# Values that are no finding of a generic rule of host-values.regex.
#
# Format: <rule> <value>, one pair for each line, the value exactly as it is in the file.
# A line that starts with "#" is a comment.
# Add a value only when it is a documentation example, a test fixture or a protocol
# constant, never an address of a real host of the publisher. This list drops no finding
# of the local deny list, so an address of the publisher's network stays a finding.
#
# Each value below is an example or a test fixture of upstream Sheprd: addresses of
# remote control, device discovery and SSH tests, the CGNAT and Tailscale ranges
# themselves, and mockup text. Commits of the upstream authors added them, and upstream
# publishes them.

